// Decides whether the software fix is viable.
//
// The firmware's own retries (SWRESET + full re-init, four times over ~1.95 s)
// cannot clear the bad panel state a cold power-on leaves behind, so the state
// needs a real RESX low pulse. RESX is tied to NRST. The question is whether
// the MCU's own reset path drives NRST low: if it does, the firmware can give
// the panel that pulse itself by resetting once after a cold boot.
//
// This writes only AIRCR.SYSRESETREQ. The J-Link's own reset line is not used,
// so anything the panel gets here comes from the MCU alone.
//
//   0x05FA0004 = VECTKEY(0x05FA) | SYSRESETREQ(bit 2)

w4 0xE000ED0C, 0x05FA0004
qc
